``` Multiple Failed Logons (burst) — Windows Security Event 4625
    Fires when a single account accumulates >= 10 failed logons
    inside any 5-minute window. Detects password guessing / brute force
    against one account, as opposed to a slow low-and-slow drip.

    Assumes the Splunk Add-on for Microsoft Windows (TA_windows) /
    CIM-normalised fields: user, host, src_ip. If your environment
    surfaces raw fields, map Account_Name -> user and
    Source_Network_Address -> src_ip first. See field-mapping.md.
```
index=wineventlog sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4625
| bin _time span=5m
| stats count as failures, dc(host) as hosts, dc(src_ip) as src_ips by user, _time
| where failures >= 10
| sort - failures
